## Definition

Assume full AC. Let $L=K_1\cup\cdots\cup K_r\subset S^3$ be a nonempty smooth oriented link, let $F$ be a connected compact smooth oriented embedded surface whose oriented boundary is $L$, and let $g$ be its genus. The compact-surface normal form gives $H_1(F;\mathbb Z)\cong\mathbb Z^{2g+r-1}$. Orient the normal line of $F$ by requiring $(n,u,v)$ to be a positive ambient frame whenever $(u,v)$ is a positive tangent frame of $F$. For an ordered integral basis $a_1,\dots,a_m$, with $m=2g+r-1$, let $a_i^+$ be its small positive normal push-off and define the Seifert matrix by $V_{ij}=\operatorname{lk}(a_i^+,a_j)$, where, for disjoint oriented cycles $J,C$, $\operatorname{lk}(J,C)$ is determined by $[J]=\operatorname{lk}(J,C)[\mu_C]$ in $H_1(S^3\setminus C;\mathbb Z)$, with $\mu_C$ the positive meridian whose oriented normal disk followed after the positive tangent to $C$ gives the ambient orientation; extend additively to cycles. The surface and basis are part of the data; this definition asserts no link-only matrix invariance.

